<title>BELGIUM: EU vets BT, Tele Danmark, UBS Swiss telecoms deal.</title>
<headline>EU vets BT, Tele Danmark, UBS Swiss telecoms deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Thursday it was starting a routine probe into a Swiss telecommunications alliance between British Telecommunications Plc, Tele Danmark A/S, Swiss Federal Railways (SBB), Union Bank of Switzerland and Swiss retailer Migros.</p>
<p>The joint company called Newtelco AG was created to take advantage of the liberalisation of the Swiss telecoms market in 1998, which is also the deadline for opening up the sector in the European Union.</p>
<p>The Commission said in a statement published in the EU's Official Journal that the deal was submitted to it for clearance on March 10 under the bloc's merger regulation which bans creation or strengthening of dominant positions in the Union.</p>
<p>The Commission has a month to clear the operation or start a full probe.</p>
<p>In a separate case, it is currently making an in-depth probe of the competition implications of an alliance between BT and MCI Corp of the United States.</p>
</text>
